      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "10,11-Epoxycarbamazepine, a polar carbamazepine metabolite, had logBB -0.33 and poor penetration; this contradictory result is attributable to the additional epoxide oxygen absent in the query and does not override the parent's lipophilic neutral profile.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "A carbamazepine-related 10-keto tricyclic showed brain/plasma ratios far below unity in mice, but the polar ketone is absent in the query and does not predict the parent's access.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "R-licarbazepine, the 10-hydroxy metabolite, had brain/plasma ratios of 0.05-0.50 in mice; the hydroxyl group increases polarity and efflux liability, unlike the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Pass. The query is carbamazepine, a neutral lipophilic tricyclic carboxamide. Supportive evidence from cyheptamide and a lipophilic benzazepine carboxamide shows that this scaffold class readily crosses the BBB. The poor-penetration records come from polar 10,11-substituted carbamazepine metabolites lacking the parent's favorable lipophilicity; bacterial meningitis would further increase CNS entry.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct carbamazepine brain/plasma or CSF measurement is present in the retrieved evidence set; the decision relies on close analogues and known pharmacology.",
    "No meningitis-specific permeability data for the query are available; extrapolation assumes inflammation-mediated BBB disruption increases entry."
  ],
